From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:18:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: drop the 32dp status_bar_height override

The framework defines status_bar_height as @dimen/status_bar_height_portrait
(values-land: status_bar_height_landscape); the V20 trees set the portrait
value to 160px, the height of the second-screen strip the camera cutout sits
in. This overlay flattened it to 32dp (112px at 560dpi) for every msm8996
device, and because msm8996-common precedes v20-common in
DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS, v20-common cannot override it.

On 22.2 that was harmless: SystemUI's qs_header_row_min_height was a fixed
48dp. In 24.0 it is @dimen/status_bar_height, so the expanded-QS header's
first row is 112px tall and the clock/date row below it starts inside the
160px cutout strip, drawing the clock under the camera. Dropping the
override restores the framework indirection and the 160px rows.

---
 .../base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml       | 25 -------------------
 1 file changed, 25 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml
deleted file mode 100644
index 05112a47..00000000
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,25 +0,0 @@
-<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
